# The one Flyway migration location. All four delivered scripts sit here flat:
# V1__create_schema.sql and V2__create_indexes.sql build the schema and its integrity layer, and
# V3__seed_reference_data.sql and V4__seed_user_security.sql seed reference rows and sign-on
# identities for local and test execution only. The flat layout is required rather than chosen - the
# migration specifications for V3 and V4 both direct that no subdirectory be created, because a
# Flyway location is scanned recursively and a directory therefore cannot isolate the seeds from the
# schema. Production is held to the schema by the version ceiling spring.flyway.target=2 instead, and
# a database that has already been seeded is refused outright by ProductionSeedRejectionCallback.
# See docs/decision-log.md DL-102 and DL-119. Do not add a subdirectory here.
